    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18222" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Firmĭus</span></b> , ii,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				Roman proper name</i>, e. g. Firmius Catus, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2,
			27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 31</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Firmĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Firmius</i>, an
			unknown silver-worker of that name: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Firmiana vasa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 11, 49, § 139</span></i>
			 (Jan. Furniana).</div>
